// EXPECT: [E085]
// LAINFLAGS: --engine=ir-full
// SOUNDNESS PAIR for the LOWER half of the relational refinement (vra_const_folding_pass.ln).
// A value's lower bound may be raised from a partner it is octagon-related to: `y - v <= c`
// with y bounded below gives `v >= ylo - c`. The same machinery must not raise a bound that
// is not there.
//
// ★ REWRITTEN 2026-09-14. This test used to read `TABLE[2] as i32 - 1` over
// `TABLE u8[4] = [10,20,30,40]` and assert a refusal, because the engine knew only u8's TYPE
// range and so read the result as [-1, 254]. Element ranges made the engine know the CONTENTS,
// at which point `30 - 1 = 29` is plainly in bounds and the refusal was no longer correct —
// the program is safe and the engine became right to accept it. Keeping the old assertion
// would have pinned an over-rejection as if it were a guarantee.
//
// The subject is preserved by giving the table a ZERO: the element range is the array-wide
// join [0, 40], so `TABLE[k] - 1` really can be -1 and `xs[j]` really can read xs[-1].
TABLE u8[4] = [0, 20, 30, 40]
proc main() i32 {
    var xs i32[256] = [0 for k in 0..256]
    var j i32 = TABLE[0] as i32 - 1
    return xs[j]
}
